From 138c5216773b9375a9fb20b3de2ddc98966d9002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:49:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: frames of graphics alone, with static
 metadata, for the menus in Dolby Vision

A frame of the menus sent in the Dolby Vision tunnel while no video plays has no picture to compose:
it is Kodi's GUI, made PQ in BT.2020 by the same LUTs that compose it over an HDR video, over black.
dvbridge_render_graphics() prepares such a frame: the full-precision transport picture is cleared to
black (and to the alpha of a pixel that nothing is drawn over) for the window system to composite the
GUI into, as it composites it over a picture, and the candidate is made over the whole raster in the
converted transport (BT.2020 YCbCr in limited range at 12 bits), which then packs it. Nothing of the
renderer's composition of pictures is touched: a picture prepared after it clears the texture again.

dvbridge_graphics.c makes the metadata of such a frame, those of a static SDR picture made PQ, and
nothing measured (ETSI GS CCM 001 V1.1.1, 6.2): the header of the converted transport; the source
display of the GUI (its white, at least the 2081 that dovi_tool keeps as the floor of a maximum of
content mapping v2.9, and its black as code 7, as dovi_tool and dvbridge_profile81_metadata() write a
mastering display of at most 0.001 cd/m2); one level 1 block that is what CCM 001 6.2.2 infers for a
frame without one (the source range and its midpoint, the average kept within dovi_tool's 819 to
max - 1); the level 5 block of the whole raster; no trims, no level 4, no content mapping v4.0. The
same bytes for every frame of the same white, so that the TV maps the menus the same way whatever
they show. CDVBridgeGLES::PrepareGraphics() keeps them for the white in use and gives the frames
times a millisecond apart, so that they follow on as one scene with one metadata id.

Checked on the host: the payload as the serializer writes it, field by field against the tables of
CCM 001 and dovi_tool's constants computed on their own, for every white of the setting; and the first
video frames after frames of the menus carry the same display-management payload as without them
(only the metadata id goes on). On a software OpenGL ES (zink on lavapipe) with Kodi's own GUI
composite shader and LUTs: every pixel that the GUI does not cover is the transport's black, the
metadata bits in the chroma are the candidate's packets, and the codes of known GUI colours are those
of a model of the pipeline within 2 codes. The render test of 1.0 RC4 draws its 156 pictures with the
same bytes before and after this change.
